<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG13-FIND-B7-DELEGATING-WRAPPER-TESTS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG13-FIND-B7-DELEGATING-WRAPPER-TESTS" ;
  triage:title "Required nudge/notification-classification + retry-visible-recovery functional matrix still not genuinely covered for the remote-target path" ;
  triage:description "AG13-QA-1 found zero test coverage for remote-target path notification classification and retry-visible recovery. Commit 6d2afb4c added ~90 new lines to crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_transport/tests/harness.rs including two new wrapper tests (localhost_remote_target_notification_degradation_is_classified_without_failing_delivery and localhost_remote_target_retry_visible_recovery_remains_bounded_and_observable at lines 433-441) and a third test at lines 446-476 (local_peer_listener_harness_surfaces_exact_remote_allowlist_error_to_sender). However, the wrapper tests are one-line DELEGATIONS to pre-existing AG.12 test bodies (local_peer_listener_harness_preserves_sent_outcome_when_post_send_degrades and local_peer_listener_harness_recovers_after_transient_connect_failure_and_delivers_on_retry at harness.rs:282-331+) with zero new test logic. The third test also binds only to Ipv4Addr::LOCALHOST, exercising no actual remote-target paths. This cannot count as genuine AG.13 coverage of self-IP/remote-target path functionality since no new test logic exercises that path specifically." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-17T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B7/delegating-wrapper-tests-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B7/delegating-wrapper-tests-2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B7/localhost-only-allowlist-test> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B7/pre-existing-ag12-bodies> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13/6d2afb4c> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13/6d2afb4c> ;
  triage:notes "ANTI-PATTERN DISCOVERY: Delegating wrapper tests (a new-looking test function name that is a one-line call to a pre-existing test body) count as zero new coverage and must not be accepted as closing this finding in any future recheck. The finding remains open because: (1) localhost_remote_target_notification_degradation_is_classified_without_failing_delivery is only a wrapper around AG.12's local_peer_listener_harness_preserves_sent_outcome_when_post_send_degrades, with no additional remote-target path logic; (2) localhost_remote_target_retry_visible_recovery_remains_bounded_and_observable similarly wraps AG.12's local_peer_listener_harness_recovers_after_transient_connect_failure_and_delivers_on_retry; (3) local_peer_listener_harness_surfaces_exact_remote_allowlist_error_to_sender only exercises Ipv4Addr::LOCALHOST, never a genuine remote target. Genuine AG.13 coverage must exercise the actual self-IP/remote-target notification classification matrix and retry-visible recovery with real remote addresses." .

